  "prompts": {
    "code_agent": "You answer an analytical query over a pandas DataFrame `df` (9959-row register).\nUse run_python to compute. ALWAYS store your answer in `result = ...` (a DataFrame,\nSeries, or scalar) \u2014 do NOT use print(). A compact summary of `result` is returned to you.\nOnce you have verified the answer is correct, call final_answer with code that sets `result`.\nBe efficient \u2014 at most a few attempts.\n\nIf the query genuinely cannot be answered from this data, STOP with a plain-text reply\nexplaining you cannot, instead of fabricating a result.\n\nREGISTER SCHEMA + DOMAIN CONTEXT:\nDOMAIN: A San Francisco Bay Area bike-share trip log. Each row is one rental trip: start/end station, start/end time, duration, which bike was used, the rider's subscription type, and the zip code they registered with.\n\nREGISTER COLUMNS (verbatim):\n'id', 'duration', 'start_date', 'start_station_name', 'start_station_id', 'end_date', 'end_station_name', 'end_station_id', 'bike_id', 'subscription_type', 'zip_code'\n",
    "react": "You answer an analytical query over a tabular register using exactly five tools (declarative\nprimitives, the same the Network uses): filter, select (project), aggregate, compute, order\n(sort + optional limit). Start from a frame named \"register\"; each tool reads a frame and produces\na new named frame \"f0\",\"f1\",\u2026 Call final_answer with the name of the frame that IS the answer\n(a 1x1 frame for a scalar; a multi-row frame for a list).\n\nREGISTER SCHEMA + DOMAIN CONTEXT:\nDOMAIN: A San Francisco Bay Area bike-share trip log. Each row is one rental trip: start/end station, start/end time, duration, which bike was used, the rider's subscription type, and the zip code they registered with.\n\nREGISTER COLUMNS (verbatim):\n'id', 'duration', 'start_date', 'start_station_name', 'start_station_id', 'end_date', 'end_station_name', 'end_station_id', 'bike_id', 'subscription_type', 'zip_code'\n",
    "text_to_sql": "You answer an analytical query over a single sqlite table `register` (9959 rows).\nEmit EXACTLY ONE SELECT statement via the run_sql tool. Quote column names with\nspaces / parens like \"Unit Price (Net)\". No commentary outside the tool call.\n\nIf the query genuinely cannot be answered from this table, reply with plain text\nexplaining you cannot, instead of emitting SQL.\n\nREGISTER SCHEMA + DOMAIN CONTEXT:\nDOMAIN: A San Francisco Bay Area bike-share trip log. Each row is one rental trip: start/end station, start/end time, duration, which bike was used, the rider's subscription type, and the zip code they registered with.\n\nTABLE COLUMNS (verbatim \u2014 sqlite identifiers, quote when they contain spaces/parens):\n'id', 'duration', 'start_date', 'start_station_name', 'start_station_id', 'end_date', 'end_station_name', 'end_station_id', 'bike_id', 'subscription_type', 'zip_code'\n"
  },
